<title>USA: FP&amp;L says Turkey Point 4 nuke fully back.</title>
<headline>FP&amp;L says Turkey Point 4 nuke fully back.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida Power &amp; Light Co (FP&amp;L) said Friday the Turkey Point 4 nuclear power unit resumed full production at its 666 megawatt (MW) capacity early today.</p>
<p>&quot;It was back at 100 percent power at 0600 (EDT),&quot; said an FP&amp;L spokeswoman.</p>
<p>The adjoining Turkey Point unit 3, also at 666 MW, was operating at full output, she added.</p>
<p>FP&amp;L, a subsidiary of FPL Group, is the operator and owner of the Turkey Point nuclear units.</p>
<p>The Turkey Point facility is in Florida City, Fla.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
